# text = Gardiner would be prevented by business from setting out till a fortnight later in July , and must be in London again within a month , and as that left too short a period for them to go so far , and see so much as they had proposed , or at least to see it with the leisure and comfort they had built on , they were obliged to give up the Lakes , and substitute a more contracted tour , and , according to the present plan , were to go no farther northwards than Derbyshire .
